Let $T\geq 3$ be a twin set in $X$, which is a maximal subset of $V(X)$ whose pairwise elements share the same neighbors. Note that $T$ is also a twin set in $X^c$. Invoking \cite[Theorem 16]{Monterde2023}, each vertex in $T$ is $(1-\frac{2}{|T|})$-sedentary in $X$ and $X^c$. Taking $C_1=C_2=1-\frac{2}{|T|}$ in Proposition~\ref{prop:NGsed}(2), we get
