Take $\lambda=\frac{-1+\sqrt{1+4\gamma}}{2}$. Similarly to the previous case, we have $\frac{\lambda^2}{\lambda^2+\gamma}=\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{1+4\gamma}}$. So, $\frac{\gamma}{\lambda^2+\gamma}=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{1+4\gamma}}>\frac{1}{2}.$ Since $\sum_{\mathbf{y}}\mathbf{y}\mathbf{y}^\top=I-\frac{1}{n}\mathbf{J}_n$, the diagonal entries of the last diagonal block of $E_{\lambda,\gamma}$ satisfy:
